@id n1_godric
# DRAFT
# Abbot Godric in the chapter house at dusk (night 1), a blanket over his knees. Frail, kind, fatherly.
# He welcomes the porter, blesses him, and speaks of the saint who keeps the house. He dreams badly (the drug; he doesn't know it).
== start
(The abbot sits on the stone bench of the chapter house with a blanket over his knees. He holds out a thin hand.)
Godric {warm}: Brother Alric. Come where I can see you. My eyes are better than Anselm's, but not by much in this light.
Godric {warm}: Welcome to our house. You're young. Good. The young sleep less and see more.
-> topics

== again
Godric {warm}: Still with an old man? The bell will ring for supper soon.
-> topics

== topics
* [if not n1_godric_blessing] Will you bless me, Father Abbot? -> blessing
* [if not n1_godric_saint] Tell me about the saint, Father Abbot. -> saint
* [if not n1_godric_porter] What would you have of your porter, Father Abbot? -> porter

== blessing [set n1_godric_blessing] [trust godric 5]
(He lays his hand on your head. It's light and cold, and it shakes.)
Godric {warm}: The Lord keep your going out and your coming in. That's the porter's psalm. I chose it for you.
-> topics

== saint [set n1_godric_saint]
Godric {calm}: Our saint has kept this house since before London had a mayor. While the relic is on the altar, nothing evil comes in.
Godric {calm}: The pilgrims come to the bone, and the bone keeps us. That's how it has always been.
Godric {afraid, look away}: Lately I dream of the saint. (He looks toward the church, and doesn't finish.) Old men dream.
-> topics

== porter [set n1_godric_porter]
Godric {grave}: Keep the gate. Ring the bell. Count us in at Matins, every one.
Godric {warm, nod}: And be kind at the grille. Half of London comes to a gate in the dark, and most of it is only cold.
-> topics

== leave
Godric {warm}: God keep your going out, brother, and your coming in.
